    "state": "{\"artifact_type\":\"code\",\"checksum\":\"sha256:7c438e7db833dfddc15534dcf90ea96da34252339631492d0319d287af533c53\",\"checksum_basis\":\"measured\",\"description\":\"The `/g/&lt;graph_id&gt;/` router — the transport half of per-session design selection, and the thing that gave Registry::discover a caller outside its own tests. A hand-written hyper/tower Service because this crate deliberately does not take axum. Holds one StreamableHttpService per design, opened ON DEMAND, with a per-id OnceCell so concurrent first requests for one design collapse into a single open rather than racing, and a cap that REFUSES past its limit rather than evicting. Isolation holds by construction: the only way to name a design is the id segment, it goes straight to Registry::attach, and each design has its own session manager so a session id minted under one prefix is unknown under another.\",\"location\":\"crates/reflow2-mcp/src/registry_http.rs\",\"name\":\"registry_http.rs\",\"status\":\"realized\"}",
